import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — the composed atom-synthesis loop (lab/mint/atom_synth_loop.py)","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/atom-synth-loop.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/atom-synth-loop.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/atom-synth-loop.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-the-composed-atom-synthesis-loop-lab-mint-atom-synth-loop-py" tabindex="-1">Retro — the composed atom-synthesis loop (<code>lab/mint/atom_synth_loop.py</code>) <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-the-composed-atom-synthesis-loop-lab-mint-atom-synth-loop-py" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — the composed atom-synthesis loop (lab/mint/atom_synth_loop.py)”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-10-14. <strong>Branch</strong>: <code>feat/atom-synth</code> (merged <code>695cd89</code>). <strong>Depends on</strong>: ADR 0007 (semantic-atom minting), <code>handler_synth</code> (layer 2), <code>lab/mint/atom_law_loop.py</code> (layer 3).</p><h2 id="what-was-built" tabindex="-1">What was built <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-was-built" aria-label="Permalink to “What was built”">​</a></h2><p><code>lab/mint/atom_synth_loop.py</code> (~1290 lines) — the five-stage composed loop the ADR-0007 layers only worked separately:</p><pre><code>measured need -&gt; candidate signature -&gt; verified handler
  -&gt; synthesized laws -&gt; certified admission -&gt; pay probe
</code></pre><ol><li><strong>Need census</strong> (live, not a stale artifact): re-exports the intake corpus (254 terms), ranks <code>invisible_ops</code> — atoms the runtime sees but no law&#39;s LHS names. Measured top needs: <code>cumsum</code> (5376 flops / 6 sites), <code>cumprod</code> (576 / 3), <code>logcumsumexp</code> (256 / 1); plus <code>pow</code> on the vocab lane and the <code>SelectiveScan</code> closed-form spec.</li><li><strong>Signature</strong>: arity/attrs read off real corpus occurrences. <strong>199 law-invisible ops have no signature builder and refuse here — that list is a deliverable, not a failure.</strong></li><li><strong>Handler</strong>: <code>handler_synth.mint_handlers</code> per spelling; ops with existing torch bindings report <code>ambient</code> (the need is the <em>law set</em>, not the body). Minted bodies bind into <code>_IR_TO_TORCH</code> so the oracle can evaluate the atom.</li><li><strong>Laws</strong>: <code>atom_law_loop._run_atom</code> verbatim, with <code>_TYPED_FAMILIES</code> / <code>_ATTR_DOMAINS</code> injected per need.</li><li><strong>Admission + pay</strong>: handler record + certified law rows + <code>cellstore</code> fragment, then a bounded default-vs-default+certified saturation on real terms.</li></ol><h2 id="what-minted-end-to-end" tabindex="-1">What minted end-to-end <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-minted-end-to-end" aria-label="Permalink to “What minted end-to-end”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong><code>scan_fold</code></strong> — the one full semantic-atom mint. The <code>SelectiveScan</code> corpus site (<code>mul(cumprod(σA), cumsum(B/clamp(cumprod(σA))))</code>) is spec&#39;d four ways; the total-form spelling mints <code>(&quot;fold&quot;,&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;,&quot;H0&quot;,-2)</code> at tried=10, err <strong>1.78e-15</strong> — the selective-scan recurrence <code>h_t = a_t·h_{t-1}+b_t</code>. Laws: 5 certified <code>primitive</code> — <code>sf.unfold</code> / <code>sf.refold</code> / <code>sf.b0</code> (auto_cond-minted guards <code>rank(a)&gt;=2</code>, <code>rank(h)&lt;=1</code>), <code>sf.split_same</code>, <code>sf.scale</code>.</li><li><strong><code>cumsum</code> / <code>cumprod</code> / <code>logcumsumexp</code></strong> — ambient handlers + certified law sets: 5/3/1 <code>primitive</code> laws each — <code>cum.add_same</code>, <code>cum.sub_same</code>, <code>cum.neg</code>, <code>cum.scale_same</code>, <code>cum.cat</code>; <code>cp.mul_same</code>, <code>cp.div_same</code>, <strong><code>cp.exp</code></strong> (the cross-atom <code>cumprod(exp x) = exp(cumsum x)</code>); <code>lc.shift_same</code>.</li><li><strong><code>pow</code></strong> — the vocab lane: the <code>2**rank</code> refusal -&gt; <code>pow</code> proposal -&gt; certified unblock (4/5 -&gt; 5/5 agreement). A separate <code>scan_needs</code> over <em>all</em> shipped rules (~470 s, run once) found <strong>zero real blocked derives</strong> — <code>pow</code> is a synthetic, not corpus, need.</li></ul><h2 id="the-stage-level-funnel-the-real-measurement" tabindex="-1">The stage-level funnel (the real measurement) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-stage-level-funnel-the-real-measurement" aria-label="Permalink to “The stage-level funnel (the real measurement)”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Signature</strong>: 199 law-invisible ops refuse — the vocabulary-gap list.</li><li><strong>Handler refusals, precisely located</strong>: <code>cumsum</code> verbatim -&gt; 0 candidates (1-meta arity floor). <code>cumsum</code> init-generalized -&gt; refused at 512; the <code>fold_emit</code> <code>a≡1</code> side is only spellable as <code>div(X,X)</code>, which the <em>disjoint</em> a/b partition can never propose, and scalar fillers (<code>1.0</code>) crash <code>broadcast_tensors</code> — dead generator space. <code>SelectiveScan</code> emitted spellings -&gt; refused at 512; the canonical <code>$acc</code> emit sits <strong>&gt;200k deep</strong> in the round-robin (the descriptor verifies at 6.7e-16 when checked directly — the gap is enumeration <em>ordering</em>, not expressiveness). The <code>clamp_min</code> domain boundary is measured: the corpus&#39;s stabilized spelling diverges from the pure fold semantics at T&gt;=32.</li><li><strong>Law refusals</strong>: bare linearity candidates -&gt; <code>rejected-undeclarable</code> (the broadcast-into-scan-axis false region; <code>auto_cond</code> can&#39;t cover &lt;=3 clauses, spelled <code>shape-compat</code> covers exactly). <code>cum.add_const</code> matches the real <code>cumsum(add(elu k,1.0))</code> site then dies on the <code>div(x,x)</code> <code>0/0</code> nan-trap. <code>sf.corpus_refold</code> matches the corpus site (<code>real=1</code>) then dies on shape — the minted atom is the fold&#39;s <em>total</em>, the corpus <em>emits</em> per-step. False twins die correctly.</li><li><strong>Pay</strong>: <strong>0 certified-law fires on every real term.</strong> The corpus&#39;s actual cumsum usages (<code>cumsum(mul(x,x))</code>, <code>cumsum(elu(k)+1)</code>, <code>cumsum(mul(unsq,unsq))</code>) all live in the guarded-out region — broadcast/product compositions, not additive splits. The guards that made the laws certifiable are exactly what correctly stops them firing on the real sites.</li></ul><h2 id="honest-read" tabindex="-1">Honest read <a class="header-anchor" href="#honest-read" aria-label="Permalink to “Honest read”">​</a></h2><p>The loop composes end-to-end mechanically — one atom minted through all four layers, four needs admitted with certified law sets. But <strong>the minted atom does not pay on the real corpus</strong>: <code>scan_fold</code> computes the total, the corpus emits the sequence (the <code>fold_emit</code> sibling is the paying one and it is enumeration-blocked); the certified cumsum laws are true but fire nowhere real because the corpus uses cumsum non-linearly. This is ADR-0007&#39;s falsification criteria working as designed: <strong>truth and pay are measured separately, and they are disjoint here.</strong></p><h2 id="issues-encountered" tabindex="-1">Issues encountered <a class="header-anchor" href="#issues-encountered" aria-label="Permalink to “Issues encountered”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>_family_gens</code> hard-gates fold/fold_emit at &gt;=3 metas — a budget heuristic, not a semantics bound (documented in the report rows).</li><li><code>fold</code>/<code>fold_emit</code> empty-side const fillers (<code>1.0</code>/<code>0.0</code>) always raise in <code>eval_body</code> — dead candidate space in the shipped grammar.</li><li><code>Provenance(origin=&quot;ambient&quot;)</code> rejected (valid origins: shipped/minted/etc.) — ambient handlers record <code>origin=&quot;shipped&quot;</code>.</li><li><code>vocab.scan_needs</code> over all shipped rules ~= 470 s; the driver defaults <code>--scan-rules 0</code> (the full-scan result: 0 blocked rules).</li></ul><h2 id="follow-ups-this-retro-produced" tabindex="-1">Follow-ups this retro produced <a class="header-anchor" href="#follow-ups-this-retro-produced" aria-label="Permalink to “Follow-ups this retro produced”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Enumeration ordering</strong> (<code>feat/enum-order</code>): reach the canonical <code>$acc</code> emit early — the fix that could flip <code>scan_fold</code> from pay-null to paying.</li><li>Grammar dead space: stop emitting candidates whose const fillers cannot evaluate.</li></ul>`,16)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};